# Line-ending and diff policy for the whole tree.
#
# The repository stores LF, so a Windows editor and the Linux CI runner agree on what "unchanged" means.
# Before this file existed the working tree picked up CRLF from local tooling while every committed blob
# was LF, so 351 files showed up as whole-file rewrites with no actual content change (`git diff
# --ignore-cr-at-eol` is empty). `text=auto` normalizes on the way in; `eol=lf` writes LF back out on
# checkout, so the churn cannot return.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Files whose bytes must survive a checkout untouched. `text=auto` normally guesses this correctly, but an
# asset that happens to look like text is the one that gets corrupted silently, so name them explicitly.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.eot    binary
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
*.tar    binary
*.nupkg  binary
*.pem    binary

# Text types git might otherwise guess wrong, forced to LF so the formatter gates (biome, tsc) and CI see
# the same bytes on every machine.
*.ts       text eol=lf
*.tsx      text eol=lf
*.js       text eol=lf
*.mjs      text eol=lf
*.cjs      text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.sql      text eol=lf
*.css      text eol=lf
*.html     text eol=lf
*.svg      text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
Caddyfile  text eol=lf
